<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Empty on purpose. AlarmKit (DawnAlarmKit.swift), the only alarm path
	     on this app's minimum iOS version, needs no entitlement at all -
	     checked against the actual installed SDK's bundled resources, nothing
	     requiring one turned up anywhere. NSAlarmKitUsageDescription in
	     Info.plist plus the runtime requestAuthorization() call is everything
	     it needs.

	     com.apple.developer.usernotifications.time-sensitive used to live
	     here, for the legacy notification fallback's interruptionLevel
	     .timeSensitive. Removed because it was added by script rather than
	     through Xcode's own Signing & Capabilities flow, leaving no matching
	     SystemCapabilities entry in project.pbxproj - that mismatch is what
	     was causing "Entitlements file was modified during the build" on
	     every few builds, as Xcode's automatic signing manager tried to
	     reconcile the two mid-build. Removing the capability removes the
	     mismatch at the root, rather than guessing at the exact
	     SystemCapabilities key Xcode expects. -->
</dict>
</plist>
